{"slug":"juiced","title":"Juiced","desc":"PC, Juice Games / THQ 2005","notes":["Read from cars/<car>.dat, carmesh.dat, cartextures.dat, carmodels.dat and scripts.dat (zlib archives; the file names are hashes, the name list is the one of Ekey's JCED.DAT.Tool).  The cars of the game's car list (scripts/cardefs.txt); folder names are the archive names, _car_names.csv gives the game's name, maker and price of each.","A car is the body (with windows, cabin and underside), the stock parts that cardefs.txt names (bonnet, front / rear bumper, side skirts, the spoiler when the car has a stock one, the stock exhaust) put on the nodes of models/<car>_stock.boh, and 4 wheels (rim, tyre and brake disc in one model) on the WHEEL nodes, which also scale them per axle (some cars have wider rear tyres).  The files hold every level of detail, this is the highest one (Juiced cars have about 3000 to 6000 triangles).","The game uses left-handed axes: the models are mirrored into right-handed ones (badges and plates read the right way; checked against an MX-5 export from 3ds Max).","Paint: the 'Car Body' material draws a picture with the panel lines and black trims over the paint colour; here over one red, like the other games.  Windows are dark glass with the black edge print of that picture; the rim spokes are cut out (the brake disc behind them shows, as in the game).","KITS: every kit part of the shop (bonnets, bumpers, side skirts, spoilers: the _vs1, _vs2 ... files) is in the hidden 'Variants' folder of <car>.fbx and, to be seen, in <car>_kits.fbx: the stock car and one complete car per kit number, all VISIBLE, in rows of 6, named kit_<n>_<brand> with the brand of cardefs.txt (wings, kaminari ...).","VINYLS: the vinyls of the shop are meshes made for each car: hidden objects in 'Variants/decal' of <car>.fbx (decal_<style>_vs<n>), not in the _kits files.  Their pictures (shared by all cars) are in _Vinyls as PNG with transparency, the sponsor stickers in _Vinyls/_sponsors.","Left out: lamp glows (lights on, brake, reverse), the empty sponsor sticker slots (the game chooses the logos at run time), motion blur wheels, the driver, shadow and collision meshes.  xrx8.dat holds the same files as rx8.dat (not repeated).  _Unused/commodore is a car that was cut from the game (only a body, no wheels).","RIMS: the folder _Rims holds the rims of the shop (wheel_<brand>_vs<n>_<size> of carmesh.dat) and the stock rim of every car (stock_<car>), each with its tyre and brake disc, one per folder, unscaled, standing on the ground, outer face towards +X.  _rims.csv: supplier and name in the shop list of the game (wheels.txt).","Known: the stock exhaust is put on the EXHAUST_S node only.  Cars with a second exhaust node (EXHAUST_O: dual exhausts) show one tip where the game has two, and the exhaust of the mr2 (a model that runs from the other node) sits beside the car."],"tags":["juiced"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["3000gt","3000GT",3366549,"juiced","car-3000gt.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-3000gt.webp"],["300zx","300Z",3884029,"juiced","car-300zx.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-300zx.webp"],["350z","350Z",3186532,"juiced","car-350z.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-350z.webp"],["ac_integra","INTEGRA TYPE R",3538614,"juiced","car-ac_integra.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-ac_integra.webp"],["ac_nsx","ACURA NSX",2140316,"juiced","car-ac_nsx.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-ac_nsx.webp"],["beetle","BEETLE GLS 1.8T",2177968,"juiced","car-beetle.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-beetle.webp"],["camaro","CAMARO",2201952,"juiced","car-camaro.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-camaro.webp"],["camaro70","CAMARO Z28",1663545,"juiced","car-camaro70.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-camaro70.webp"],["celica","CELICA SS-I",4793159,"juiced","car-celica.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-celica.webp"],["celica_2","CELICA SS-II",3426140,"juiced","car-celica_2.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/car-celica_2.webp"],["charger","1969 CHARGER R/T",1696770,"juiced","car-charger.zip","thumbs/juiced/cars/ca